{"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "rop", "ucas": "it(d: u8) = d + 1\nrop it model fixed", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "rop", "update": "d + 1", "model": "fixed", "order": "immaterial", "forms": [{"family": "stencil op", "state": "VK_STENCIL_OP_INCREMENT_AND_WRAP on the 8-bit stencil value: d + 1", "proof": "checked on every point of the domain", "class": "rop_stencil", "available": true, "cost": 3, "against": 144.5, "cheaper": true, "pipeline": "VkStencilOpState: passOp = VK_STENCIL_OP_INCREMENT_AND_WRAP, writeMask = 0xff; a stencil attachment (S8_UINT); one fragment per contribution, its position the cell"}, {"family": "occlusion query", "state": "VK_QUERY_TYPE_OCCLUSION, precise, around the draw: the fragments that pass, counted: d + 1", "holds_where": "every contribution updates the same cell: a query counts a whole draw (more cells: a draw and a query each)", "proof": "the update is d + 1 (checked on every point of the domain); a precise occlusion query counts every sample that passes the fragment tests, which with no depth or stencil test and one sample a point is one a contribution; read as 64 bits the count is exact, and adding it to the cell wraps in u8 as the update does", "class": "rop_query", "available": false, "pipeline": "VkQueryPoolCreateInfo: queryType = VK_QUERY_TYPE_OCCLUSION; vkCmdBeginQuery with VK_QUERY_CONTROL_PRECISE_BIT (the occlusionQueryPrecise feature) around a draw of one point per contribution, anywhere (no depth or stencil test, one sample a pixel); vkCmdCopyQueryPoolResults with VK_QUERY_RESULT_64_BIT into a buffer, and the cell's d + count once after the draw"}], "count": 2}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "rop it: it = d + 1, applied once per fragment (d the cell's value)\n  order: every fragment applies the same update: their order is immaterial\n  fixed-function states that compute it (each a proposal: the pipeline changes):\n  stencil op: VK_STENCIL_OP_INCREMENT_AND_WRAP on the 8-bit stencil value: d + 1\n      checked on every point of the domain\n      price: rop_stencil 3 a fragment under fixed, against 144.5 (a global compare-and-swap around the update: atomic_global_cas 143.5 + 1): cheaper\n      pipeline: VkStencilOpState: passOp = VK_STENCIL_OP_INCREMENT_AND_WRAP, writeMask = 0xff; a stencil attachment (S8_UINT); one fragment per contribution, its position the cell\n  occlusion query: VK_QUERY_TYPE_OCCLUSION, precise, around the draw: the fragments that pass, counted: d + 1\n      holds where every contribution updates the same cell: a query counts a whole draw (more cells: a draw and a query each)\n      the update is d + 1 (checked on every point of the domain); a precise occlusion query counts every sample that passes the fragment tests, which with no depth or stencil test and one sample a point is one a contribution; read as 64 bits the count is exact, and adding it to the cell wraps in u8 as the update does\n      price: rop_query is not priced by fixed (not measured): unavailable\n      pipeline: VkQueryPoolCreateInfo: queryType = VK_QUERY_TYPE_OCCLUSION; vkCmdBeginQuery with VK_QUERY_CONTROL_PRECISE_BIT (the occlusionQueryPrecise feature) around a draw of one point per contribution, anywhere (no depth or stencil test, one sample a pixel); vkCmdCopyQueryPoolResults with VK_QUERY_RESULT_64_BIT into a buffer, and the cell's d + count once after the draw\n  not in any price: the draw's setup (a render pass, the pipeline, one vertex per contribution) and reading the target back\n"}
{"id": 5, "ok": true, "cmd": "rop", "ucas": "it(s: u32, d: u32) = d * 3 + s\nrop it", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "rop", "update": "3d + s", "model": "gt1030", "order": "dependent", "count": 0}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "rop it: it = 3d + s, applied once per fragment (s what a fragment brings, d the cell's value)\n  order: the result depends on the order of the fragments (it(s2, it(s1, d)) is not it(s1, it(s2, d))): a draw applies them in primitive order, atomics in any\n  no fixed-function state in the catalogue computes it (logic ops, stencil ops, the blend equation with its factors, min, max, the advanced blend operations, the depth test, an occlusion query)\n"}
{"id": 6, "ok": true, "cmd": "rop", "ucas": "it(s: u64, d: u64) = min(d, s)\nrop it", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "rop", "update": "min(d, s)", "model": "gt1030", "order": "independent", "order_proof": "proved by SAT", "forms": [{"family": "depth test", "state": "VK_COMPARE_OP_LESS on a D32_SFLOAT depth attachment holding the key s >> 35, the payload s & 0x7ffffffff in an R32G32_UINT colour attachment written where the test passes: min(s, d)", "holds_where": "two values that meet in a cell differ in their keys, or come in increasing order of payload (the payload the contribution's index in the draw: a cell's fragments pass in primitive order); the keys below 0x3F000000 (at most 536870911, from the parameters' ranges)", "proof": "the test keeps s >> 35 < d >> 35 ? s : d, which is min(s, d) wherever the keys differ or the new payload is the larger (proved by SAT); on a tie the test keeps the cell, and min keeps the smaller payload, hence the order; a key's depth is the f32 whose bits are key + 2^23, normal, in [2^-126, 1) and increasing with the key, so the depth compare is the keys' integer compare and nothing rounds", "class": "rop_depth", "available": false, "pipeline": "VkPipelineDepthStencilStateCreateInfo: depthTestEnable, depthWriteEnable, depthCompareOp = VK_COMPARE_OP_LESS; a D32_SFLOAT depth attachment and an R32G32_UINT colour attachment (blending off), cleared to (or copied from) the cells' keys and payloads; one point per contribution, its position the cell, gl_FragDepth = uintBitsToFloat(uint(s >> 35) + 0x00800000), its colour s & 0x7ffffffff; the cell's value is (key << 35) | payload, the key the depth's bits - 0x00800000"}], "count": 1}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "rop it: it = min(d, s), applied once per fragment (s what a fragment brings, d the cell's value)\n  order: the result does not depend on the order of the fragments: it(s2, it(s1, d)) = it(s1, it(s2, d)) (proved by SAT)\n  fixed-function states that compute it (each a proposal: the pipeline changes):\n  depth test: VK_COMPARE_OP_LESS on a D32_SFLOAT depth attachment holding the key s >> 35, the payload s & 0x7ffffffff in an R32G32_UINT colour attachment written where the test passes: min(s, d)\n      holds where two values that meet in a cell differ in their keys, or come in increasing order of payload (the payload the contribution's index in the draw: a cell's fragments pass in primitive order); the keys below 0x3F000000 (at most 536870911, from the parameters' ranges)\n      the test keeps s >> 35 < d >> 35 ? s : d, which is min(s, d) wherever the keys differ or the new payload is the larger (proved by SAT); on a tie the test keeps the cell, and min keeps the smaller payload, hence the order; a key's depth is the f32 whose bits are key + 2^23, normal, in [2^-126, 1) and increasing with the key, so the depth compare is the keys' integer compare and nothing rounds\n      price: rop_depth is not priced by gt1030 (not measured): unavailable\n      pipeline: VkPipelineDepthStencilStateCreateInfo: depthTestEnable, depthWriteEnable, depthCompareOp = VK_COMPARE_OP_LESS; a D32_SFLOAT depth attachment and an R32G32_UINT colour attachment (blending off), cleared to (or copied from) the cells' keys and payloads; one point per contribution, its position the cell, gl_FragDepth = uintBitsToFloat(uint(s >> 35) + 0x00800000), its colour s & 0x7ffffffff; the cell's value is (key << 35) | payload, the key the depth's bits - 0x00800000\n  not in any price: the draw's setup (a render pass, the pipeline, one vertex per contribution) and reading the target back\n"}
{"id": 7, "ok": true, "cmd": "rop", "ucas": "it(x: i32 in 0..63, y: i32 in 0..63) = x > y\nrop it", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "rop", "predicate": "x > y", "model": "gt1030", "forms": [{"family": "rasterisation", "state": "a convex polygon of 3 vertices drawn over the grid (1 triangle as a fan), its coverage it(x, y)", "holds_where": "the grid's pixels are the framebuffer's, x and y their coordinates", "proof": "its edges cover a pixel's centre exactly where it holds (checked on every point of the domain) and pass through no centre (checked on every point of the domain), so the rasteriser's tie rule never decides; the vertices are multiples of 1/16, Vulkan's coarsest sub-pixel grid (subPixelPrecisionBits >= 4), so no device moves them; a centre on one of the fan's diagonals is in exactly one of its triangles", "class": "rop_raster", "available": false, "pipeline": "a draw of 1 triangle as a fan over the window positions (0.5, 0), (64, 0), (64, 63.5) (pixel (x, y) is the framebuffer's: x and y below maxFramebufferWidth and Height), no culling, a viewport covering the grid; the fragment shader runs on the pixels where it holds, instead of a test in every invocation"}], "count": 1}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "rop it: it(x, y) = x > y, a predicate of the pixel (x, y) over [0, 63] x [0, 63]\n  fixed-function states that compute it (each a proposal: the pipeline changes):\n  rasterisation: a convex polygon of 3 vertices drawn over the grid (1 triangle as a fan), its coverage it(x, y)\n      holds where the grid's pixels are the framebuffer's, x and y their coordinates\n      its edges cover a pixel's centre exactly where it holds (checked on every point of the domain) and pass through no centre (checked on every point of the domain), so the rasteriser's tie rule never decides; the vertices are multiples of 1/16, Vulkan's coarsest sub-pixel grid (subPixelPrecisionBits >= 4), so no device moves them; a centre on one of the fan's diagonals is in exactly one of its triangles\n      price: rop_raster is not priced by gt1030 (not measured): unavailable\n      pipeline: a draw of 1 triangle as a fan over the window positions (0.5, 0), (64, 0), (64, 63.5) (pixel (x, y) is the framebuffer's: x and y below maxFramebufferWidth and Height), no culling, a viewport covering the grid; the fragment shader runs on the pixels where it holds, instead of a test in every invocation\n  not in any price: the draw's setup (a render pass, the pipeline, 3 vertices)\n"}
